<title>GERMANY: Postbank says has not signed pact with post office.</title>
<headline>Postbank says has not signed pact with post office.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Postbank AG on Tuesday said it had not signed a cooperation agreement with the German post office, or Post AG, and said a decision would be reached by the end of April.</p>
<p>Earlier, the post office had said it had signed the agreement, which was drafted by Germany's post ministry after talks between the two state-owned companies had failed.</p>
<p>Postbank also said it would hold an extraordinary supervisory meeting on April 30.</p>
